{
  "about": "A two-layer v2 envelope (core §2.1-§2.3, §3.2 L2, §3.3; FS §2.5): layer 1 to the recipient's epoch key, layer 2 to its interaction key in the interaction (ikid = KID(1, pub), info {1: \"anet-ix/v2\", 2: to, 3: 1, 4: ikid}); Wrap {1 ikid, 2 enc2, 3 layer-2 ciphertext, 21 pad} on a Padmé length; the inner, unpadded, signed over the preimage v2 with 33 = ikid and 34 = enc2. The outer carries a capability access (kind 1: CapBody signed by the recipient's mailbox key, holder proof over env_digest), key 8 equal to the inner exp and the extension key 64; the inner carries rk and the extension key 64 and none of keys 10, 11, 12, 14 (the seal layer does not tie keys to a type; the daemon does). Written by gen_v016.py with the ephemeral keys DeriveKeyPair(seed(\"ikmE\")) for layer 1 and DeriveKeyPair(seed(\"ikmE2\")) for layer 2; the Go test derives both recipient keys from their seeds and opens the bytes. single_layer is the same message sealed as one layer under the same layer-1 ephemeral key: its ack_key is the same (FS-C14). The body is opaque to the seal layer.",
  "seeds": "seed(role) = SHA-256(\"anet-golden/v016/SEALED-2B/<role>\"); Ed25519 keys are the seeds, X25519 keys are DeriveKeyPair(seed) of RFC 9180 suite 1",
